% 10_tie_and_slur.mus -- audible test: ties (no retrigger) vs. detached
% repeats, and a slurred phrase vs. the same phrase unslurred.
%
% A tied leaf (~) sends no MIDI note-off (core.async-engine's
% send-midi-off! skips it when :tied is true), so the two notes read as
% one continuous sound; contrast against the same two notes without a
% tie, which each get their own attack. A tie also makes a nice probe
% for onset-timing: a dynamic change written right at the join point
% takes effect exactly there, since the second (untied) leaf samples its
% own volume at its own onset -- audible as a level jump mid-phrase.

{tie_vs_retrigger:
  !mf
  C4/2~ C4/2
  r4
  C4/2 C4/2
}

{tie_spans_a_dynamic_change:
  !mf
  C4/1~
  !ff
  C4/1
}

{slur_legato_vs_unslurred:
  !mf
  C4/4( d e f g f e d)
  r4
  C4/4 d e f g f e d
}
